<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Item enchantments (Diablo style). Only items with a rarity (or unique) have enchantment slots, the amount of slots of
	each rarity is configured in config.lua (enchantSlots*).
	An enchantment is applied by using its item (here the old runes, which can not be cast anymore) on the item to be
	enchanted: the item is consumed (one unit) and the enchantment becomes permanent. The look of the item shows the enchantments
	and the free slots.
	<enchantment>
		name: name shown in the look of the item (can not have ";").
		item: id of the item that applies the enchantment (one enchantment per item id).
		types: kinds of item that can receive it, separated by comma:
			all, weapon (sword, club, axe, distance, wand and fist), sword, club, axe, distance, shield, fist, wand,
			head, armor, legs, feet, necklace, ring, ammo, backpack.
		effect: (optional) magic effect shown on the player when the item is enchanted.
		<attribute name="..." value="N"/>: bonus of the enchantment, any attribute of rarity_attributes.xml.
			attack, defense and armor are added to the item itself, all the others work while the item is equipped.
-->
